  "howItWorksParagraphs": [
    {"name": "the info dialog spells out the all-correct gaps", "out": [
      "Each day you get the words that are due, plus a few new ones (choose how many in Settings). Spell each one from its definition and an example.",
      "Spaced repetition brings a word back just before you'd forget it. Each time you spell it right first try, the gap before you see it again grows.",
      "Right first try every time, a word comes back after 1 day, then 6 days, 17 days, 49 days, 147 days, and then once a year.",
      "Get it wrong, even if you then retype it correctly, and it comes back tomorrow and climbs again from the start, a little more slowly than before.",
      "Longer gaps move a day or so either way, so words added together don't all come due at once. A word counts as known once its gap reaches three weeks."
    ]}
  ],
